A||||5||Two88GTs||Finally changed the TCC solenoid - PITA!||||7||
Z||000000||Two88GTs||06-07-2001||01:16 AM||||Kudos to everyone that changed their own TCC solenoid with a Delco unit AND managed to plug in the last polarized connector near the top of the side tranny pan.  I could barely get my fingers on it.  As a matter of fact I nearly shed tears of joy when I heard the connector click into place.  Maybe now I can count on getting better mileage on the highway.  I think I cured the slow tranny fluid leak too as the side tranny pan bolts were too loose for comfort.   ||||reg||7
Z||000001||mrfiero||06-07-2001||01:58 AM||||I just did this on my low mileage GT......for some reason it failed at 14K miles.  I knew it would be a PITA, so I put it off for over a year (now has 16K miles).<P>It took me about an hour to finally get it plugged in.....I could only get my thunb and forefinger in between the TV cable, so it was a SLOW process (as you well know).<P>Congratulations on a successful job....pat yourself on the back and have a beer or two with the $$$ you saved by doing it yourself.  <P>I haven't put many miles on the GT since I did the repair, so I can't say how my mileage was affected (but I imagine it'll go up a bit on the freeway).||||reg||10
Z||000002||84Bill||06-07-2001||07:56 AM||||I never even disconnected mine. The old one was bad so I just cut the wire and since the new one has those clippy on wire splicee things, installing the new one was a snap.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Brucepts||06-07-2001||08:07 AM||||Hey 84Bill since you have some experience doing this why don't you come on over to my place and you can show me how to do mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> My 84 should be the same as yours so it should be a snap for you to do LOL<P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||06-07-2001||08:16 AM||||Mine also had the splice connectors and wasn't too bad.  The not so fun part was scraping the gasket off the side of the trans case.||||reg||1
